 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk about the future",
   "texto": [
    "**Skal + infinitivo** expresses a plan: **Jeg skal flytte** («I'm moving out.»). After **skal** it does not put **å**. **Vil + infinitivo** expresses will or intention: **Jeg vil begynne** («I want / I'm gonna start»).",
    "The Norwegian can use the same way to talk about the future that the Spanish expresses with «go to» or with the present; the context clarifies whether it is plan or intention."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk about objectives",
   "texto": [
    "**Planlegger å + infinitivo** means «planeo…». **Ønsker å + infinitivo** means «I want to» or «deseo…». In Spanish it is sometimes used «that + subjunctive»; in Norwegian it follows the infinitive with **å**."
   ]
  },
